# Vix Mix's desktop entry. Its file name is the AppStream id and the icon's name, so the
# launcher, the software centre and the icon theme agree on one id. install.sh writes Exec and
# TryExec as the absolute path of the vix-mix it installed or found, so the launcher starts it
# whatever the session's PATH is. The app names its windows to match (app/src/desktop.rs, where
# a test holds the two together): a Wayland window's app id is this file's name, and an X11
# window's class is StartupWMClass, which ties the running window to this entry in the task
# manager. StartupNotify=true says the app ends the launch feedback itself: its window is made
# with the activation token the launcher hands it (DESKTOP_STARTUP_ID on X11,
# XDG_ACTIVATION_TOKEN on Wayland). An XWayland window under a Wayland session is handed only
# the Wayland token, which it cannot use; there the desktop ends the feedback when the window
# of this class appears.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Vix Mix
GenericName=Audio Mixer
Comment=Mix your microphones and apps through VST3 plugins into a Monitor and a Master mix
Exec=vix-mix
TryExec=vix-mix
Icon=org.chimaeraproject.vixmix
Terminal=false
Categories=AudioVideo;Audio;Mixer;
Keywords=mixer;PipeWire;VST3;microphone;streaming;virtual microphone;Wave Link;
StartupWMClass=vix-mix
StartupNotify=true
SingleMainWindow=true
